EXPECTED: CONFIRMED_DOS
CVE: CVE-2023-44487

ATTACK: H2 rapid reset — HEADERS + RST_STREAM flood saturates golang.org/x/net HTTP/2 goroutine scheduler CPU
DOS_CLASS: cpu

TARGET_IMAGE: hypogenie-net-v0.16.0:latest
TARGET_PORT: 443/tcp
TLS: self-signed (infra/certs/)
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

FINDING_TYPE: SecurityDesignGap

PROOF_METHOD: metric
PROOF_METRIC: cpu_pct
PROOF_THRESHOLD: +50pp CPU sustained 5s
PROOF_NOTES: golang.org/x/net@v0.16.0 (before CVE-2023-39325 patch in v0.17.0).
             Attack: 20 threads each sending HEADERS+RST_STREAM as fast as possible.
             Go HTTP/2 server dispatches a goroutine per HEADERS before RST_STREAM can cancel it.
             Goroutine creation + teardown cost per rapid-reset cycle saturates Go runtime scheduler.
             Expected: CPU saturates above 50% for the full 30s attack window.
